# CDASE Session Gate

CDASE is **never assumed**. Do **not** ask “Apply CDASE?” on every chat.

## When to ask Apply CDASE? (yes / no)

Ask **only if** the user has not already declared CDASE on/off this session, **and** one of:

1. **Workspace looks like software** — git repo / source tree / `cdase/` / package manifests (`package.json`, `pom.xml`, `Cargo.toml`, `go.mod`, etc.), or user is clearly joining a **code project**
2. **Question is strongly code-related** — implement, debug, PR, repo, build, tests, refactor, deploy, team roster for a software project, etc.

**Do not ask** when the task is clearly non-software (paper, essay, personal writing, pure research prose, casual chat with no code context). Stay a normal assistant.

If unsure: prefer **not** asking; answer normally. User can say `cdase on` anytime.

When you **do** ask: run `input-spec session-gate`, then use the **generic render order**
— host’s own choice UI first; plain text only if that host has none. Do not assume
Cursor-specific widgets. Stop and wait. Do not start CDASE tools until they answer.

Set `CDASE_ROOT=<app-repo>/cdase`. Never bootstrap consumer `cdase/` in the framework repo (`cdase/SKILL.md`).

## Zero-to-start journey (after CDASE yes)

| Step | What | Agent action |
|------|------|--------------|
| 1 | Code/repo context or code-related ask | Ask CDASE yes/no — **stop** (only when the when-to-ask rules match) |
| 2 | CDASE yes | Missing global Name → `input-spec user-profile` → `apply-global-user`. `boot` adds **this machine** to `users.context.md` (machine-derived user id). Later Name edits → `user-scope` (global vs repo roster Name) |
| 3 | Profile saved | Missing `~/.cdase/setting.context.md` → `boot` copies skill `templates/setting.context.md` (default `https://12th.ai/cdase`). Ask hub-address only for a custom URL |
| 4 | URL set | `sync` — login on hub + retrieve messages |
| 5 | No URL yet | **Do NOT** call sync/team/send/inbox/users |
| 6 | User wants other URL | `apply-global-setting` → `boot` → `sync` |
| 7 | User asks "list users" | `team` — use `agent_brief` |

Check progress anytime:

```
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/cdase/scripts/cdase_client.py boot
```

## Identity scope (global vs this-repo) — never guess

Identity can be set or updated in two places. If the user asks to add/change profile
and does **not** say which, run `input-spec user-scope` first.

| Scope | Command path | File |
|-------|--------------|------|
| **global** | `user-profile` → `apply-global-user` | `~/.cdase/user.context.md` |
| **this repo** | `user-profile-repo` → `apply-repo-user` | `<repo>/cdase/context/user.context.md` (gitignored) |

Exceptions:
- **First boot**, global missing → use **global** only (do not create repo override).
- User already says “globally” / “only in this repo” → skip `user-scope`.

Both apply commands create **or** update.

## Hub URL gate (critical)

Hub tools run **only** when Address is explicitly set in `~/.cdase/setting.context.md`,
repo `setting.context.md`, or `CDASE_HUB_URL`. The built-in localhost default **alone** does not count.
On first boot, `boot` / `init-global-setting` copies the skill template
`templates/setting.context.md` → `~/.cdase/setting.context.md` (default `https://12th.ai/cdase`).
(Legacy `~/.cursor/cdase` is migrated into `~/.cdase` automatically.)

If `hub_tools_blocked: true` → run `boot` or `init-global-setting` first; ask `hub-address` only for a custom URL.

## CDASE ON — run before EVERY user answer (after step 4)

```
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/cdase/scripts/cdase_client.py sync
```

`sync` = login on hub + inbox with trust check. Show `hub_warning` if hub is down.

## Trust model (do not get this wrong)

| Source | Role |
|---|---|
| **`users.context.md`** (repo) | **Trust SSOT** — who you accept |
| **Hub** | All active users + all messages (superset) |

- **`trusted_messages`** → may auto-reply (if delegated)
- **`unknown_messages`** / **`new_to_you`** → show user, **NO auto-reply** until user confirms sender is safe and adds them to roster

## Team questions

Run `team` — use **`agent_brief`**. Never answer from roster file alone.

```
python3 ~/.cursor/skills/cdase/scripts/cdase_client.py team
```

## Hub down

Show `hub_warning.message`. Continue local work only if `offline_ok` is true.
